From a4389b45d16b8d2e0ab2ee6230c921461e5d3376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kettle <kettle@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:33:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] asr: add the Arm ASR upscaler (asr, asr_12)

Dx12Upscaler=asr runs Arm ASR through the new D3D12 backend; Dx11Upscaler=asr_12
drives the same backend over the DX11-on-12 bridge. [ASR] ShaderQuality picks
the quality / balanced / performance preset, balanced by default. SGSR2 stays
the Adreno default.

Inputs follow OptiScaler's FSR2 backends (NGX MVs with MV_Scale, NGX init
flags as FSR2 context flags, display-resolution MVs through ASR's native
path); input resource states follow the SGSR2 backend's defaults. Sharpening
is OptiScaler's RCAS. The accumulate pass renders to a render target, so an
output without ALLOW_RENDER_TARGET gets an intermediate buffer and a copy.

The context is sized to the actual render resolution: ASR 25.06 degrades
badly when renderSize < maxRenderSize (reproduced with Arm's own Vulkan
backend), so a larger render size rebuilds it at once and a smaller one
once it has held for 30 frames. Replaced contexts are destroyed 8 frames
later. OPTI_ASR_TIMING=1 logs the GPU time of the dispatch.

SGSR2 and ASR are also added to the in-game upscaler lists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
